\section{Related work}\label{sec:related}

PyTorch's own shape ecosystem
(\verb|torch.fx|+\verb|ShapeProp|~\citep{rink2018hindley},
\verb|FakeTensorMode|, \verb|torch.export|, and the
\verb|ShapeEnv| of
\verb|torch.fx.experimental.symbolic_shapes|) is execution-based
and value-level (\Cref{tab:tools}); none of these tools have a
notion of static abstention or formal soundness on uninstantiable
source. Earlier static work on PyTorch and on Hindley-Milner
shape inference (\citealp{rink2018hindley,rush2019tensor}) is
type-system-based and non-executive but does not produce
counterexample witnesses or address the helper-built-Sequential
indirection. Abstract interpretation of array programs has a long
history~\citep{cousot1977abstract}; \textsc{TensorGuard}
specialises the framework to the typed AST fragment of
\texttt{nn.Module} forwards and adds a Lean-verified core for the
operator transfer functions.

\section{Limitations}\label{sec:limitations}

\textsc{TensorGuard} is a verifier for a typed AST fragment, not
for arbitrary PyTorch. (i) It abstains on opaque submodules
passed in as constructor arguments, on helper-built
\texttt{Sequential}s whose layer dims depend on opaque
computation, and on data-dependent control flow inside the
forward method; the abstain rate on real-source torchvision is
$19/30$ (\Cref{tab:tv-source}). (ii) The Lean-verified core
covers $11$ representative operators; the analyzer wires $30+$
additional handlers (\Cref{app:ops-extended}) whose soundness
proofs are pen-and-paper. (iii) RNN/LSTM/GRU recurrence and
custom \verb|autograd.Function| classes are out-of-fragment.
(iv) The divisibility checker for \texttt{view(-1,\ldots)} is
complete only on the linear-Diophantine fragment, not on general
polynomial divisibility (\Cref{app:floor-divisibility}).

\section{Conclusion}\label{sec:conclusion}

\textsc{TensorGuard} demonstrates that a typed-AST fragment of
PyTorch \texttt{nn.Module} forward methods is a usable target for
sound static shape verification: zero false positives on $30$
real torchvision sources, zero shape-rejections on six real-repo
files, F$_1=1.00$ on a curated buggy/safe suite, and a
machine-checked Lean core. The cost is an honest abstention
verdict on subgraphs that exit the fragment.

