\section{Detailed soundness proof}\label{sec:soundness-proof}
The proof of \Cref{thm:soundness} is by induction on the number
of trace steps. The base case (empty trace, output is the input
shape) is immediate. The inductive case for an in-fragment
operator $f$: by hypothesis, all input abstract shapes
$s_1,\ldots,s_k$ correctly over-approximate the concrete operand
shapes; by the per-operator transfer-function lemmas
(\Cref{sec:lean-theorems}, $11$ Lean-verified instances) the
output abstract shape over-approximates the concrete output
shape. The inductive case for an out-of-fragment construct: the
analyzer substitutes the bottom element (fresh symbolic shape),
which over-approximates every concrete shape vacuously, so the
soundness invariant is preserved. The result follows.

