\section{Floor and divisibility for \texttt{Conv2d} and
\texttt{view(-1, \ldots)}}\label{app:floor-divisibility}

\paragraph{\texttt{Conv2d} output spatial size.} For
\verb|Conv2d(C_i, C_o, k, stride=s, padding=p, dilation=d)| with
input shape $(B, C, H, W)$, PyTorch computes
$H' = \lfloor (H + 2p - d(k-1) - 1)/s \rfloor + 1$. We represent
$H'$ symbolically as a pair $(\alpha, \beta)$ where $\alpha = H +
2p - d(k-1) - 1 \in \mathbb Z[\mathcal V]$ and $\beta = s \in
\mathbb Z_{>0}$. Two such symbolic floors are equal iff
$\alpha_1\beta_2 = \alpha_2\beta_1$ as polynomials and
$\beta_1 = \beta_2$. Soundness: if $\alpha_1 = c\beta_1$ exactly,
then $\lfloor\alpha_1/\beta_1\rfloor + 1 = c + 1$ for every
integer instantiation. When $\alpha_1 \bmod \beta_1$ is not
provably zero, the analyzer attaches a divisibility precondition
that downstream operators must discharge before equality can be
claimed; if the downstream demand is the linear Diophantine
constraint $\alpha_1 = e\beta_1$, the analyzer either proves it
by canonical-form normalization or fails sound (\textsf{abstain}).

\paragraph{\texttt{view(-1, e\_2, \ldots, e\_m)}.} A view with
one $-1$ entry resolves the missing dim as $\prod_i d_i / \prod_{j>1}
e_j$. We replace $-1$ with a fresh symbolic dim $u$ and emit the
precondition $\prod_i d_i = u\cdot\prod_{j>1}e_j$. If the
canonical form admits a solution in $u$, $u$ is replaced by the
quotient and propagation proceeds; otherwise the verifier emits
\textsf{rejected} with the failed equation as witness. The check
is decidable on the polynomial fragment when one side is a
constant times the other; residual cases return \textsf{abstain}.
We do not claim completeness over general polynomial divisibility
(NP-hard).

